WEBVTT

1
00:01.250 --> 00:09.620
Now we're going to look at our first big O and I start with O of N, not because it is the most efficient

2
00:09.620 --> 00:16.610
or least efficient big O, but because I think it's the easiest to explain, easiest one to get your

3
00:16.610 --> 00:17.450
head around.

4
00:17.750 --> 00:20.630
So we're going to explain this with some code.

5
00:21.020 --> 00:25.100
So we're going to create a function that we're going to call print items.

6
00:25.400 --> 00:28.220
We're going to pass it a number n.

7
00:28.670 --> 00:33.350
And we're going to have a for loop that runs in times.

8
00:33.350 --> 00:37.880
And then we're going to print I from the for loop.

9
00:37.880 --> 00:38.900
Pretty simple.

10
00:38.900 --> 00:43.790
So let's flip over to VS code and have a look at this.

11
00:44.720 --> 00:45.110
Okay.

12
00:45.110 --> 00:46.910
So there is our function.

13
00:46.910 --> 00:49.550
And then we're going to call it here with the number ten.

14
00:49.550 --> 00:50.900
So I'm going to run this.

15
00:51.750 --> 00:55.770
And you can see over here that it printed out zero through nine.

16
00:55.770 --> 00:59.490
So there were ten items that were printed to the screen.

17
00:59.490 --> 01:01.050
So let's flip back.

18
01:01.050 --> 01:05.820
So this is an example of something that is O of n.

19
01:05.820 --> 01:08.460
We passed it the number n.

20
01:09.150 --> 01:11.790
And then it ran in time.

21
01:11.790 --> 01:13.800
So we're in operations.

22
01:14.220 --> 01:17.250
So whatever N was, that was the number of operations.

23
01:17.250 --> 01:18.510
So that's O of N.

24
01:18.660 --> 01:21.420
Let's take a look at this on a graph.

25
01:22.710 --> 01:27.150
So on this graph on this bottom axis, that's n.

26
01:27.360 --> 01:32.010
And on the other axis this is the number of operations.

27
01:32.010 --> 01:37.050
So o of n is always going to be a straight line.

28
01:37.050 --> 01:39.810
It is what is called proportional.

29
01:39.810 --> 01:46.170
So if you hear the word proportional when it comes to big O that is going to be O of n.

30
01:46.620 --> 01:51.600
So we'll be adding to this graph so we can compare one to another.

31
01:51.750 --> 01:55.230
But for now that is O of n.
